[tadah hpo] the STRATEGY-level optimiser: CERES:STEEPEST_DESCENT ignores the OPTIM box: Ceres' line-search solver has no bounds, so its line searches can propose points outside the box (a LOG dimension stays positive, a linear one is unbounded). Such a point is not evaluated. It is scored as a failure graded by its distance to the box, so the score rises away from the box and a descent step leads back into it. Such a point counts against MAXEVAL and is never the best. The first is reported with a WARNING; the DIAGNOSTICS section of hpo_run.log counts them all. DLIB:BFGS and the NLopt LD_* algorithms keep to the box
